# MoE conventions

## Terminology (use exactly)

| Term | Meaning |
|---|---|
| **EP** | Expert Parallelism (experts sharded across ranks) |
| **TP** | Tensor Parallelism (each expert's weights sharded) |
| **DP** | Data Parallelism |
| **PP** | Pipeline Parallelism |
| **Dispatch** | All-to-all that sends tokens to their assigned experts |
| **Combine** | All-to-all that returns expert outputs back to source ranks |
| **Permute** | Local rearrangement before/after dispatch |
| **FC1 / FC2** | First / second linear of an MoE expert MLP |
| **Drop** | Capacity-based token dropping (capacity_factor < ∞) |
| **Top-K** | Routing top-k (do not abbreviate to just "K") |

Always use these names; do not invent synonyms.

## Where to look first

| Question | File |
|---|---|
| What does an MoE forward look like end-to-end? | `knowledge/moe/dataflow.md` |
| What parallelism combinations exist? | `knowledge/moe/research-directions.md` |
| What did paper X say? | `papers/<slug>.md` |
| What experiments have we run on monolithic MoE kernel? | `notes/monolith-moe/README.md` (timeline) |

## When writing a new MoE paper note

- Filename: `papers/<slug>.md` (slug omits "moe" suffix when the project
  itself includes it, e.g. `comet.md` not `comet-moe.md`).
- Must include: problem, contribution, method (with a dataflow sketch),
  experiments, limitations, our take. See
  `.cursor/skills/read-paper/SKILL.md` or `paper-deep-analysis/SKILL.md`.
- Update `papers/README.md` index table (Year | Title | Tags |
  One-liner | File).

## When writing a monolith-moe progress note

- Filename: `notes/monolith-moe/YYYY-MM-DD_HHMM_<topic>.md`.
- Append a row to the timeline in `notes/monolith-moe/README.md`.
- Use `.cursor/skills/progress-note/SKILL.md`.
